/-!
# Quantitative equidistribution of weights modulo the root lattice

Let `L` be a finite-dimensional semisimple Lie algebra over an algebraically closed field of
characteristic zero, `H` a Cartan subalgebra, `b` a base of its root system, `Q` the root lattice
and `φ : Q → A` a surjection onto a finite commutative group. For `m ≥ 1` let `M` be a
finite-dimensional module generated by a highest weight vector of weight `2 m · 2ρ`, `2ρ` the sum
of the positive roots. Pushing the weight multiplicities of `M` forward along `φ` and dividing by
`dim M` gives a probability distribution `p_m` on `A`, and this file proves that it approaches the
uniform distribution at rate `1 / m`:

`∑_{a ∈ A} |p_m(a) - 1 / |A|| ≤ C / m`,

with `C` depending on `φ` but on neither `m` nor `M`. In type `A₁` with `A = ℤ/2` the masses at
`m = 1` are `3/5` and `2/5`, at distance `1/5` from uniform.

## The argument

The character of `M` is the product `∏_{α>0} ∑_{j=-2m}^{2m} e^{j α}` of centred root strings
(`TauCeti.formalCharacter_eq_prod_sum_Icc`), all of whose exponents lie in `Q`, and
`dim M = (4 m + 1) ^ |Φ⁺|`. Pushed forward to `ℤ[A]`, the Fourier coefficient of `p_m` at a
character `ψ` of `A` is `∏_{α>0} (4 m + 1)⁻¹ ∑_{j=-2m}^{2m} ψ(φ α)^j`. As `φ` is onto and the roots
generate `Q`, a nontrivial `ψ` has `ψ(φ α) ≠ 1` at some positive root `α`; that factor is a
geometric sum of norm at most `2 / ‖1 - ψ(φ α)‖`, divided by `4 m + 1`, and the other factors have
norm at most `1`. The `ℓ¹` distance to the uniform distribution is at most the sum of the
nontrivial Fourier coefficients (`TauCeti.sum_norm_sub_mean_le_sum_norm_fourier`).

## Main results

* `TauCeti.weightPushforward_sum_abs_sub_uniform_le`: **quantitative equidistribution of the
  weights of the modules of highest weight `2 m · 2ρ`** modulo a finite quotient of the root
  lattice.

## References

* C. Fu, *Stability of elliptic Fargues–Scholze L-packets*, arXiv:2501.00652, Lemma 3.1.2 and the
  proof of Proposition 3.3.1.
* D. Hansen, *Excursion operators and the stable Bernstein center*, Forum Math. Pi 14 (2026),
  proof of Lemma 2.6, where the rate `1 / m` is used.
-/

public section

namespace TauCeti

open AddMonoidAlgebra Finset LieAlgebra LieModule Module

/-! ### Pushing weights forward to a finite quotient of the root lattice -/

variable {K : Type*} {L : Type*} [Field K] [CharZero K] [IsAlgClosed K]
  [LieRing L] [LieAlgebra K L] [IsKilling K L] [FiniteDimensional K L]
  {H : LieSubalgebra K L} [H.IsCartanSubalgebra]
  {A : Type*} [AddCommGroup A]

/-- A root, as an element of the root lattice. -/
private noncomputable abbrev rootLatticeRoot (i : H.root) :
    AddSubgroup.closure (Set.range (IsKilling.rootSystem H).root) :=
  ⟨(IsKilling.rootSystem H).root i, AddSubgroup.subset_closure ⟨i, rfl⟩⟩

/-- The product `∏_{α>0} ∑_{j=-n}^{n} e^{j φ(α)}` of the root strings pushed forward to `ℤ[A]`. -/
private noncomputable def rootStringProduct (b : (IsKilling.rootSystem H).Base) (n : ℕ)
    (φ : AddSubgroup.closure (Set.range (IsKilling.rootSystem H).root) →+ A) :
    AddMonoidAlgebra ℤ A :=
  ∏ i ∈ posRootsFinset (IsKilling.rootSystem H) b,
    ∑ j ∈ Icc (-(n : ℤ)) n, single (j • φ (rootLatticeRoot i)) 1

open scoped Classical in
/-- The pushforward of the weight multiplicities of a module of highest weight `n · 2ρ` along
`φ : Q → A` is the coefficient of the product `∏_{α>0} ∑_{j=-n}^{n} e^{j φ(α)}` in `ℤ[A]`. -/
private theorem pushforward_eq_coeff_prod {M : Type*} [AddCommGroup M] [Module K M]
    [LieRingModule L M] [LieModule K L M] [FiniteDimensional K M]
    {b : (IsKilling.rootSystem H).Base} {n : ℕ} {v : M}
    (hv : IsHighestWeightVector b (n • twoWeylVector (IsKilling.rootSystem H) b) v)
    (hgen : LieSubmodule.lieSpan K L {v} = ⊤)
    (φ : AddSubgroup.closure (Set.range (IsKilling.rootSystem H).root) →+ A) (a : A) :
    ((formalCharacter K H M).coeff.sum fun χ c ↦
        if h : χ ∈ AddSubgroup.closure (Set.range (IsKilling.rootSystem H).root) then
          (if φ ⟨χ, h⟩ = a then (c : ℝ) else 0) else 0) =
      ((rootStringProduct b n φ).coeff a : ℝ) := by
  -- The character lifts to `ℤ[Q]`, and the product is the image of that lift in `ℤ[A]`.
  set c : AddMonoidAlgebra ℤ (AddSubgroup.closure (Set.range (IsKilling.rootSystem H).root)) :=
    ∏ i ∈ posRootsFinset (IsKilling.rootSystem H) b,
      ∑ j ∈ Icc (-(n : ℤ)) n, single (j • rootLatticeRoot i) 1
  have hch : formalCharacter K H M = mapDomainRingHom ℤ
      (AddSubgroup.closure (Set.range (IsKilling.rootSystem H).root)).subtype c := by
    simp [formalCharacter_eq_prod_sum_Icc hv hgen, c, map_prod, map_sum, mapDomain_single]
  have hP : rootStringProduct b n φ = mapDomainRingHom ℤ φ c := by
    simp [rootStringProduct, c, map_prod, map_sum, mapDomain_single]
  rw [hch, hP]
  clear_value c
  clear hch hP
  induction c using AddMonoidAlgebra.induction_linear with
  | zero => simp
  | add x y hx hy =>
    simp only [map_add, coeff_add, Finsupp.add_apply, Int.cast_add, ← hx, ← hy]
    exact Finsupp.sum_add_index' (fun _ ↦ by simp) fun _ _ _ ↦ by split_ifs <;> simp
  | single q r => simp [mapDomain_single, coeff_single, Finsupp.single_apply]

/-- The Fourier coefficient at `ψ` of the product of root strings in `ℤ[A]` is the product of the
geometric sums `∑_{j=-n}^{n} ψ(φ α)^j`. -/
private theorem sum_coeff_mul_addChar_prod [Fintype A] (ψ : AddChar A ℂ)
    (b : (IsKilling.rootSystem H).Base) (n : ℕ)
    (φ : AddSubgroup.closure (Set.range (IsKilling.rootSystem H).root) →+ A) :
    ∑ x, ((rootStringProduct b n φ).coeff x : ℂ) * ψ x =
      ∏ i ∈ posRootsFinset (IsKilling.rootSystem H) b,
        ∑ j ∈ Icc (-(n : ℤ)) n, ψ (φ (rootLatticeRoot i)) ^ j := by
  -- Both sides are the evaluation `e^x ↦ ψ x`, a ring homomorphism `ℤ[A] → ℂ`.
  set ev := AddMonoidAlgebra.lift ℤ ℂ A ψ.toMonoidHom
  have hev (f : AddMonoidAlgebra ℤ A) : ev f = ∑ x, (f.coeff x : ℂ) * ψ x := by
    rw [AddMonoidAlgebra.lift_apply, Finsupp.sum_fintype _ _ fun _ ↦ by simp]
    simp [zsmul_eq_mul]
  rw [← hev]
  simp [ev, rootStringProduct, map_prod, map_sum, AddMonoidAlgebra.lift_single,
    AddChar.map_zsmul_eq_zpow]

/-- A nontrivial character of `A` is nontrivial on the image of some positive root, the roots
generating the root lattice and `φ` being onto. -/
private theorem exists_mem_posRootsFinset_addChar_ne_one {ψ : AddChar A ℂ}
    (hψ : ψ ≠ 0) (b : (IsKilling.rootSystem H).Base)
    {φ : AddSubgroup.closure (Set.range (IsKilling.rootSystem H).root) →+ A}
    (hφ : Function.Surjective φ) :
    ∃ i ∈ posRootsFinset (IsKilling.rootSystem H) b, ψ (φ (rootLatticeRoot i)) ≠ 1 := by
  by_contra! hpos
  -- A negative root is the negative of a positive one.
  have hroot (i : H.root) : ψ (φ (rootLatticeRoot i)) = 1 := by
    rcases mem_posRoots_or_mem_negRoots (IsKilling.rootSystem H) b i with hi | hi
    · exact hpos i ((mem_posRootsFinset _ b i).mpr hi)
    · have hj := hpos _ ((mem_posRootsFinset _ b _).mpr
        ((reflectionPerm_self_mem_posRoots_iff_mem_negRoots _ b i).mpr hi))
      have hneg : rootLatticeRoot ((IsKilling.rootSystem H).reflectionPerm i i) =
          -rootLatticeRoot i := by
        refine Subtype.ext ?_
        rw [AddSubgroup.coe_neg]
        exact (RootPairing.root_reflectionPerm _ _ _).trans (RootPairing.reflection_apply_self _ _)
      rwa [hneg, map_neg, AddChar.map_neg_eq_inv, inv_eq_one] at hj
  -- Run the induction in the root lattice, generated by the roots it contains.
  have hall (q : AddSubgroup.closure (Set.range (IsKilling.rootSystem H).root)) :
      ψ (φ q) = 1 := by
    have hq : q ∈ AddSubgroup.closure (((↑) : AddSubgroup.closure
        (Set.range (IsKilling.rootSystem H).root) → Dual K H) ⁻¹'
          Set.range (IsKilling.rootSystem H).root) := by
      rw [AddSubgroup.closure_closure_coe_preimage]
      exact AddSubgroup.mem_top q
    induction hq using AddSubgroup.closure_induction with
    | mem x hx =>
      obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := hx
      rw [show x = rootLatticeRoot i from Subtype.ext hi.symm]
      exact hroot i
    | zero => rw [map_zero, AddChar.map_zero_eq_one]
    | add x y _ _ ihx ihy => rw [map_add, AddChar.map_add_eq_mul, ihx, ihy, one_mul]
    | neg x _ ihx => rw [map_neg, AddChar.map_neg_eq_inv, ihx, inv_one]
  refine hψ (AddChar.ext _ _ fun x ↦ ?_)
  obtain ⟨q, rfl⟩ := hφ x
  rw [hall q, AddChar.zero_apply]

/-- The bound on the Fourier coefficient at `ψ` of the normalized root-string product, before
dividing by the string length: the sum of `2 / ‖1 - ψ(φ α)‖` over the positive roots `α` with
`ψ(φ α) ≠ 1`. -/
private noncomputable def charBound (b : (IsKilling.rootSystem H).Base)
    (φ : AddSubgroup.closure (Set.range (IsKilling.rootSystem H).root) →+ A)
    (ψ : AddChar A ℂ) : ℝ :=
  ∑ i ∈ posRootsFinset (IsKilling.rootSystem H) b,
    if ψ (φ (rootLatticeRoot i)) = 1 then 0 else 2 / ‖1 - ψ (φ (rootLatticeRoot i))‖

private theorem charBound_nonneg (b : (IsKilling.rootSystem H).Base)
    (φ : AddSubgroup.closure (Set.range (IsKilling.rootSystem H).root) →+ A)
    (ψ : AddChar A ℂ) : 0 ≤ charBound b φ ψ :=
  sum_nonneg fun _ _ ↦ by split_ifs <;> positivity

/-- At a nontrivial character `ψ`, the product of the root strings, each divided by its length
`2 n + 1`, has norm at most `charBound ψ / (2 n + 1)`: one factor is a geometric sum with ratio
`ψ(φ α) ≠ 1`, and the others have norm at most `1`. -/
private theorem norm_prod_inv_mul_sum_Icc_le [Finite A] {ψ : AddChar A ℂ} (hψ : ψ ≠ 0)
    (b : (IsKilling.rootSystem H).Base)
    {φ : AddSubgroup.closure (Set.range (IsKilling.rootSystem H).root) →+ A}
    (hφ : Function.Surjective φ) (n : ℕ) :
    ‖∏ i ∈ posRootsFinset (IsKilling.rootSystem H) b,
        ((2 * n + 1 : ℂ)⁻¹ * ∑ j ∈ Icc (-(n : ℤ)) n, ψ (φ (rootLatticeRoot i)) ^ j)‖ ≤
      charBound b φ ψ / (2 * n + 1) := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨i₀, hi₀, hz⟩ := exists_mem_posRootsFinset_addChar_ne_one hψ b hφ
  have hd : (0 : ℝ) < 2 * n + 1 := by positivity
  have hfactor (i : H.root) :
      ‖(2 * n + 1 : ℂ)⁻¹ * ∑ j ∈ Icc (-(n : ℤ)) n, ψ (φ (rootLatticeRoot i)) ^ j‖ =
        ‖∑ j ∈ Icc (-(n : ℤ)) n, ψ (φ (rootLatticeRoot i)) ^ j‖ / (2 * n + 1) := by
    rw [norm_mul, norm_inv, div_eq_inv_mul]
    congr 2
    exact_mod_cast Complex.norm_natCast (2 * n + 1)
  rw [norm_prod, ← mul_prod_erase _ _ hi₀]
  refine (mul_le_of_le_one_right (norm_nonneg _) (prod_le_one₀ (fun _ _ ↦ norm_nonneg _)
    fun i _ ↦ ?_)).trans ?_
  · rw [hfactor, div_le_one hd]
    exact norm_sum_Icc_zpow_le_two_mul_add_one (ψ.norm_apply _) n
  · rw [hfactor]
    gcongr
    unfold charBound
    refine (norm_sum_Icc_zpow_le (ψ.norm_apply _) hz n).trans (le_of_eq_of_le ?_
      (single_le_sum (fun _ _ ↦ by split_ifs <;> positivity) hi₀))
    simp [hz]

/-- The Fourier coefficient at `ψ` of the root-string product divided by its total mass
`(2 n + 1) ^ |Φ⁺|` is the product of the normalized geometric sums. -/
private theorem sum_coeff_div_mul_addChar [Fintype A] (ψ : AddChar A ℂ)
    (b : (IsKilling.rootSystem H).Base) (n : ℕ)
    (φ : AddSubgroup.closure (Set.range (IsKilling.rootSystem H).root) →+ A) :
    ∑ x, ((((rootStringProduct b n φ).coeff x : ℝ) /
        (2 * n + 1 : ℝ) ^ (posRootsFinset (IsKilling.rootSystem H) b).card : ℝ) : ℂ) * ψ x =
      ∏ i ∈ posRootsFinset (IsKilling.rootSystem H) b,
        ((2 * n + 1 : ℂ)⁻¹ * ∑ j ∈ Icc (-(n : ℤ)) n, ψ (φ (rootLatticeRoot i)) ^ j) := by
  rw [prod_mul_distrib, prod_const, ← sum_coeff_mul_addChar_prod ψ b n φ, mul_sum]
  refine sum_congr rfl fun x _ ↦ ?_
  push_cast
  ring

/-- **Equidistribution of the root-string product.** Divided by its total mass
`(2 n + 1) ^ |Φ⁺|`, the root-string product in `ℤ[A]` is within `∑_{ψ ≠ 0} charBound ψ / (2 n + 1)`
of the uniform distribution in `ℓ¹`. -/
private theorem sum_abs_coeff_div_sub_uniform_le [Fintype A] (b : (IsKilling.rootSystem H).Base)
    {φ : AddSubgroup.closure (Set.range (IsKilling.rootSystem H).root) →+ A}
    (hφ : Function.Surjective φ) (n : ℕ) :
    ∑ a : A, |((rootStringProduct b n φ).coeff a : ℝ) /
        (2 * n + 1 : ℝ) ^ (posRootsFinset (IsKilling.rootSystem H) b).card -
          1 / (Fintype.card A : ℝ)| ≤
      (∑ ψ ∈ univ.erase (0 : AddChar A ℂ), charBound b φ ψ) / (2 * n + 1) := by
  set f : A → ℂ := fun x ↦ ((((rootStringProduct b n φ).coeff x : ℝ) /
    (2 * n + 1 : ℝ) ^ (posRootsFinset (IsKilling.rootSystem H) b).card : ℝ) : ℂ)
  -- The trivial character sees the total mass, which is `1`.
  have hmass : ∑ x, f x = 1 := by
    have h := sum_coeff_div_mul_addChar 0 b n φ
    simp only [AddChar.zero_apply, mul_one, one_zpow] at h
    rw [h, prod_eq_one fun i _ ↦ ?_]
    rw [sum_const, Int.card_Icc_neg_natCast_natCast, nsmul_eq_mul, mul_one]
    push_cast
    exact inv_mul_cancel₀ (by exact_mod_cast Nat.succ_ne_zero (2 * n))
  have hdist := sum_norm_sub_mean_le_sum_norm_fourier f
  rw [hmass] at hdist
  calc _ = ∑ a, ‖f a - 1 / Fintype.card A‖ := sum_congr rfl fun a _ ↦ by
        rw [← Real.norm_eq_abs, ← Complex.norm_real]
        simp [f]
    _ ≤ _ := hdist
    _ ≤ ∑ ψ ∈ univ.erase (0 : AddChar A ℂ), charBound b φ ψ / (2 * n + 1) :=
        sum_le_sum fun ψ hψ ↦ (sum_coeff_div_mul_addChar ψ b n φ).symm ▸
          norm_prod_inv_mul_sum_Icc_le (ne_of_mem_erase hψ) b hφ n
    _ = _ := (sum_div ..).symm

open scoped Classical in
/-- **Quantitative equidistribution of weights modulo the root lattice.** Let `m ≥ 1` and let
`M` be a finite-dimensional module generated by a highest weight vector of weight `2m · 2ρ`, where
`2ρ` is the sum of the positive roots of the base `b`; such an `M` is the irreducible module of
dimension `(4m + 1) ^ N`, `N` the number of positive roots. Push the weight multiplicities of `M`
along a surjection `φ` from the root lattice onto a finite commutative group `A` and divide by
the dimension of `M`. The `ℓ¹` distance from the uniform distribution on `A` is at most `C / m`,
with `C` depending on `φ` but not on `m` or `M`. -/
theorem weightPushforward_sum_abs_sub_uniform_le
    (b : (IsKilling.rootSystem H).Base) [Fintype A]
    (φ : AddSubgroup.closure (Set.range (IsKilling.rootSystem H).root) →+ A)
    (hφ : Function.Surjective φ) :
    ∃ C : ℝ, 0 ≤ C ∧ ∀ m : ℕ, 1 ≤ m →
      ∀ (M : Type*) [AddCommGroup M] [Module K M] [LieRingModule L M] [LieModule K L M]
        [FiniteDimensional K M] (v : M),
        IsHighestWeightVector b
          ((2 * m : ℕ) • twoWeylVector (IsKilling.rootSystem H) b) v →
        LieSubmodule.lieSpan K L {v} = ⊤ →
        ∑ a : A, |((formalCharacter K H M).coeff.sum fun χ n ↦
            if h : χ ∈ AddSubgroup.closure (Set.range (IsKilling.rootSystem H).root) then
              (if φ ⟨χ, h⟩ = a then (n : ℝ) else 0) else 0) / (finrank K M : ℝ)
            - 1 / (Fintype.card A : ℝ)| ≤ C / m := by
  have hC := sum_nonneg fun ψ (_ : ψ ∈ univ.erase (0 : AddChar A ℂ)) ↦ charBound_nonneg b φ ψ
  refine ⟨(∑ ψ ∈ univ.erase (0 : AddChar A ℂ), charBound b φ ψ) / 4, by positivity,
    fun m hm M _ _ _ _ _ v hv hgen ↦ ?_⟩
  -- `M` has dimension `(4 m + 1) ^ |Φ⁺|`, the total mass of the root-string product.
  have hdim : (finrank K M : ℝ) =
      (2 * (2 * m : ℕ) + 1 : ℝ) ^ (posRootsFinset (IsKilling.rootSystem H) b).card := by
    rw [nsmul_twoWeylVector] at hv
    exact_mod_cast finrank_eq_pow_card_posRootsFinset hv hgen
  simp_rw [pushforward_eq_coeff_prod hv hgen φ, hdim]
  refine (sum_abs_coeff_div_sub_uniform_le b hφ (2 * m)).trans ?_
  have : (1 : ℝ) ≤ m := by exact_mod_cast hm
  rw [div_div]
  exact div_le_div_of_nonneg_left hC (by positivity) (by push_cast; linarith)

end TauCeti
